# ANTLR4 tool jar downloaded by cmake into external/
external/antlr-*-complete.jar

# Object files
*.o
*.ko
*.obj
*.elf

# Libraries
*.lib
*.a

# Shared objects (inc. Windows DLLs)
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# Executables. Name the OUTPUT_NAMEs, not the CMake target names: `tonto`,
# `hart` and `rgbi` are what actually land on disk. The old rules here named
# run_molecule/run_har, the targets -- which is why three built binaries were
# committed inside foofiles/ and nothing stopped them. Since ffebb767 the
# program target is itself called `tonto`.
tonto
hart
rgbi
run_molecule
run_har
*.exe
*.out
# ... except blessed test references. tests/hart/ jobs are argv-driven, so they
# name their own output (<job>.out) instead of writing a file called "stdout".
!tests/*/*/*.out
*.app
*.i*86
*.x86_64
*.hex

# An IN-SOURCE build inside foofiles/. This is not hypothetical: 1554 such
# files -- the translator's .F90/.int/.use, binary .mod, CMakeFiles/ and the
# linked executables -- reached master in b292b121 and had to be removed from
# history. The generated Fortran belongs in the build tree; a stale
# foofiles/crystal.F90 beside foofiles/crystal.foo is exactly the confusion
# CLAUDE.md SS8 forbids. scripts/check_foofiles_clean.sh asserts the end state,
# because an ignore rule alone is defeated by `git add -f`.
#
# Scoped to foofiles/ deliberately: .F90/.int/.use are the translator's output
# there, but the out-of-source trees are covered separately below and runfiles/
# is a different case.
foofiles/*.F90
foofiles/*.int
foofiles/*.use
foofiles/*.F90.d
foofiles/CMakeFiles/
foofiles/CMakeCache.txt
foofiles/cmake_install.cmake
foofiles/CTestTestfile.cmake

# Fortran module files and CMake stamps, wherever they land. Nothing legitimate
# in this repository is named either.
*.mod
*.stamp

# Build Files
Makefile
foodependencies/
# Out-of-source CMake build trees. Any build*/ directory: the convention is
# build/ for release and build-debug/ alongside it (CLAUDE.md SS8 -- probe in a
# debug build, keep the release tree for the reference runs).
build*/
build

# ...and the other out-of-source trees that exist in working copies. These were
# committed by accident in 646078a0 (6553 files, 2.7M lines; that
# commit was 58314cb6 before the 2026-08-04 history rewrite that stripped the
# blobs out again) and untracked
# again straight after; they are regenerable and must never be tracked.
release/
debug/
mpi/
antlr4-release/
release-gfortran14/
debug-gf14/

# Temporary test files
*.bad
# `make report` writes this into the build directory, but a hand-run of
# suite_report.py in the repo root leaves one here.
/tests.log
# tonto/hart open a file literally called "stderr" in the working directory,
# so a hand-run in the repo root leaves one behind (this is also why so many
# test IO manifests list "delete: stderr").
/stderr

# Plaforms Specific Build Files
GNU-*
IBM-*
INTEL-*
MIPSPRO-*
NAG-*
PGI-*
PATHSCALE-*
SUN-*

# Mac Specific Files
.DS_Store

# cscope/ tags files
tags
cscope.*

# vim swap files
.*.swp

# Krita files & backups
lg-movie.kra
lg-movie.kra~
*.bmp
*.kra
*.kra~
*movie*
*~


# Python bytecode from running the test/report scripts in-tree
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code: .claude/settings.json and .claude/hooks/ are shared (they carry
# the unsynced-work hook, which is wanted on every machine); the local settings
# file is per-machine permissions and is not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The CRYSTAL23 wavefunction for tests/long/ammonium_borane_pHAR_C23, 167 MB.
# Fetched on demand by scripts/fetch_phar_asset.sh; the asset lives on the tag
# archive/release-pHAR-broken and must NOT be committed here. Committing it, or
# committing its LFS pointer with a .gitattributes that tracks it, would make
# every clone of this repository pull 167 MB. `git lfs ls-files develop` must
# stay empty.
tests/long/ammonium_borane_pHAR_C23/GenerateXML.XML

# Untracked by design, and both were swept into a commit by a careless `git add -A`
# on 2026-08-26 (caught and amended out before pushing).
#
# external/sbf: Peter Spackman's sbf. It was REMOVED as a submodule on 2026-08-11 --
# nothing in CMakeLists.txt or cmake/*.cmake ever referenced it, so it was neither
# compiled nor linked. A working copy may still sit here; it must not come back into
# the index. See docs/TONTO_REPOSITORY_BRANCHES.md.
external/sbf/

# A local Python virtualenv for the RGBI picture scripts -- machine-specific,
# hundreds of files, and it has absolute paths baked into its bin/ scripts.
rgbi-scripts/.venv/
.venv/
